I have to watch an ad for there's an ad for board shorts that used to play at the beginning of like every surf line video from five years ago ago that I will never forget, but you just watch it because you're like, well, I got to see the cam and you do that until one day you're fed up and you transition over.

475
00:36:46,400 --> 00:36:49,200
But I might be an interesting case because you talk about that propensity to pay.

476
00:36:49,280 --> 00:36:51,200
Like, I can afford a Surfline subscription, right?

477
00:36:51,440 --> 00:36:55,120
There's probably some users who never do or it's never going to be a thing they do.

478
00:36:55,600 --> 00:37:00,960
And not to steal your answer, Paul, but like David, I don't even know if that's necessary totally, right?

479
00:37:01,200 --> 00:37:06,480
Like the value of a premium user base has value and ideally you want to set it up to have value in itself.

480
00:37:06,720 --> 00:37:09,600
You convert them great, but they also provide word of mouth.

481
00:37:10,160 --> 00:37:11,120
They also provide feedback.

482
00:37:11,280 --> 00:37:13,680
In Surfline's case, you guys also monetize with advertising.

483
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:15,760
So they provide a base you monetize from as well.

484
00:37:16,160 --> 00:37:19,520
So yeah, before we're on the spot, like, are you actually making money on these people?

